# The Contested Space of Prudence in the 1874-1875 Civil Rights Debate.

**Authors:** Wilson, Kirt H.

## Abstract
Contributes to scholarship on rhetorical theory and political judgment theory by examining how the rhetoric of Reconstruction congressional actors expressed divergent modes of political judgment regarding the civil rights of African Americans. Contends that proponents and opponents enacted adverse norms of discursive practice and competing conceptions of equality. (SR)

